{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace_ne_naive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace_ne_naive","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/corrected_markov_trace.lean#L55-L69","doc":"**Naive vs corrected**: the trefoil Markov trace is NOT the naive\nvertex-volume product `h·z² + z` (whenever those two scalars differ).\n\nCombines `corrected_markov_trace` with the inequality hypothesis\n`z³ ≠ h·z² + z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/corrected_markov_trace.lean#L28-L53","doc":"**Corrected Markov-trace of the trefoil** `tr_M(σ₀ σ₁ σ₀) = z³`,\nderived from the Markov reduction steps.\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly the three reduction steps of the `.md`\nproof, each an instance of the Markov property (peel the maximal-index\ngenerator, multiplying the trace by `z`):\n\n* `h_single : trM_σ0 = z`               (single generator),\n* `h_reduce1 : trM_σ1σ0 = z * trM_σ0`   (peel `σ₁`),\n* `h_reduce2 : trM_σ0σ1σ0 = z * trM_σ1σ0` (peel the top `σ₀`).\n\nFrom these, `tr_M(σ₀σ₁σ₀) = z·(z·(z)) = z³` by substitution and\n`ring`.  None of the hypotheses asserts the conclusion `= z³`.\n\n**Base ring (§7c).** The reduction recursion is a polynomial identity\n(`z·z·z = z³`) — only `+`, `*`, substitution, and a `≠` distinctness\nhypothesis; no inverse, no `Real.*`, no ordering. It is therefore stated\nover a generic commutative ring `{R : Type*} [CommRing R]`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:corrected-markov-trace","label":"prop:corrected-markov-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/corrected-markov-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}